* ''Test and collide canon'' (operator, 2026-11-07: //"apply the 5th commandment of the pentabarf (don't just beleieve everything, test and collide. We grew this system and its docs FAST and there's bound to be stale leftovers or places where the deisgn and code drifted but one feels most pono). If uncertainty spikes and can't be talked out, do a 'Luna class, 2 wave research pass'"//). A ruling or a brief that rests on a canon claim measures the code first; on drift the most pono side stands and both sides are named. A spike that the talk-out cannot settle takes a two-wave read (one breaks the claim, one collides the first), then the talk-out.

